<main class="public-composition public-composition--about container" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <section class="about-help-set">
    <div class="about-help-set__about"><span class="eyebrow">About Kurukoo</span><h1 id="about-title">About Kurukoo</h1><p>Kurukoo is a conversation-first assistant that helps you find clarity, prepare requests and move work forward using the sources you already trust.</p><div class="about-help-set__principles"><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#chat"></use></svg><div><strong>Built around conversation</strong><span>Ask naturally and get answers that understand context and intent.</span></div></article><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#discover"></use></svg><div><strong>Grounded in your sources</strong><span>Answers use connected sources so you can verify and go deeper.</span></div></article><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#safety"></use></svg><div><strong>Private by design</strong><span>Your data stays private and you remain in control of what’s connected.</span></div></article></div></div>
    <div class="about-help-set__help"><span class="eyebrow">Help</span><h2>Find answers and get support.</h2><div class="about-help-set__help-list"><a href="/help"><span><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#chat"></use></svg></span><div><strong>Getting started</strong><small>Learn the basics and start your first conversation.</small></div><b>›</b></a><a href="/help"><span><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#channels"></use></svg></span><div><strong>Connecting your sources</strong><small>Step-by-step guides for each provider.</small></div><b>›</b></a><a href="/help"><span><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#settings"></use></svg></span><div><strong>Account &amp; privacy</strong><small>Manage your account, data, and preferences.</small></div><b>›</b></a><a href="/help"><span><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#package"></use></svg></span><div><strong>Billing &amp; plans</strong><small>Learn about seats, plans, and billing.</small></div><b>›</b></a></div><aside class="about-help-set__support"><strong>Still need help?</strong><p>Our team is here for you.</p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/contact">Contact support</a></aside></div>
  </section>
  <section class="public-narrative-card"><div><span class="eyebrow">The Kurukoo relationship</span><h2>One place to ask, organise and continue.</h2><p>Kurukoo keeps useful context connected as a conversation develops. Requests, reminders, discovery and supported coordination remain part of the same relationship rather than separate destinations.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/chat">Start with the conversation</a></div><div class="public-conversation-preview" aria-label="Illustrative Kurukoo conversation"><span class="public-conversation-preview__label">Kurukoo</span><p class="public-conversation-preview__user">I’ll come back to this later.</p><p class="public-conversation-preview__agent">That’s okay. The useful context can stay connected for when you return.</p><small>Illustrative conversation preview</small></div></section>
  <section class="public-detail-grid" aria-label="How Kurukoo works">
    <article class="public-detail-card"><span class="eyebrow">Beyond the bot</span><h2>Orchestrate the useful next step.</h2><p>Kurukoo is a fulfillment and orchestration network, not a collection of disconnected dashboards. Conversation keeps the request, context and supported next action together.</p><p>Payment, catalogue, delivery and provider actions remain conditional on the required data, authorization and integrations being available.</p></article>
    <article class="public-detail-card"><span class="eyebrow">Trust as a boundary</span><h2>Known states stay known.</h2><p>Identity, provider information, evidence and payment states are requested or shown only when their corresponding boundary is available.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works">See how request states work →</a></article>
  </section>
</main>
